# ==========================
# OS / Base Image Issues
# ==========================

# ncurses fix blocked by glibc upgrade requirement, waiting for backport or fix in next Debian stable release.
CVE-2025-6141
CVE-2025-69720

# zlib - CPU consumption/DoS vulnerability. Fixed in zlib 1.3.2. Waiting for backport or fix in next Debian stable release.
CVE-2026-27171

# Hidden File Injection in tar — mitigate by not extracting untrusted tar files.
CVE-2026-5704

# Privilege escalation and symlink traversal / out-of-bounds write in tar. Waiting for fix to be released by tar maintainers.
CVE-2026-18477
CVE-2026-18508

# Hostname spoofing in util-linux. Waiting for fix in unstable - fix might only be possible in next Debian stable release.
CVE-2026-3184

# Out-of-bounds write in libc. Waiting for fix in unstable - risks with backporting / upgrading glibc - fix might only be possible in next Debian stable release.
CVE-2026-5435

# DNS Verification Bypass in libc. Waiting for fix in unstable - risks with backporting / upgrading glibc - fix might only be possible in next Debian stable release.
CVE-2026-6238

# perl vulnerabilities - waiting for fixes to be released by perl maintainers or in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-9538

# Symlink traversal in acl. Fix released by acl maintainers - waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-54370
CVE-2026-54369

# Symlink traversal in attr. Fix released by attr maintainers - waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-54371

# Denial of Service in bzip2. Waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-42250

# Timing discrepancy / Plaintext password recovery in linux-pam. Only exploitable when pam_userdb is configured with crypt=none.
CVE-2026-54411

# Null pointer reference / Denial of Service, and Information disclosure in libsqlite3. Fixed in sqlite3 3.53.2-1 - waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-50812
CVE-2026-50813

# Path traversal / arbitrary process termination in systemd-oomd, and local privilege escalation in systemd-homed (libudev1). Not exploitable in this image - systemd-oomd/systemd-homed are not present/running in this container. Fix only available in forky/sid.
CVE-2026-15059
CVE-2026-16742

# Arbitrary code execution / OOB memory access in perl regex engine (perl-base). Not reachable via any code path in this image (Perl not invoked as a service). Waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-15534

# Heap buffer overflow via fopen ccs=, buffer overflow in strfmon, out-of-bounds write in tdelete, process abort/DoS and stack exhaustion in wordexp, and infinite loop/hang in iconv SHIFT_JISX0213/EUC_JISX0213 conversion (libc). None of these code paths are used by the Python stdlib or in this image. Waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-18374
CVE-2026-19499
CVE-2026-19542
CVE-2026-6368
CVE-2026-6791
CVE-2026-77117
CVE-2026-80489

# Privilege escalation via unchecked mount post-hooks, nsenter --join-cgroup cgroup migration authority leak, X-mount.subdir symlink traversal, and bind mount source redirection in util-linux. Not applicable to this image - no fstab-based mount workflow or nsenter usage; runs as non-root entrypoint. Waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410

# Stack overflow / DoS in nscd via oversized DNS response (libc). Not exploitable in this image - nscd is not installed/running. No fix currently available upstream.
CVE-2026-89092

# Heap buffer overflow in zlib (1.3.1.2-1.3.2). No upstream fix released yet (Debian bug #1146895). zlib is used broadly for compression/decompression (including via Python's zlib module) - flagged for re-assessment once an upstream/Debian fix lands.
CVE-2026-85091

# Denial of Service (assertion failure/process abort) in glibc DNS stub resolver via long search domain in resolv.conf. Requires an attacker-influenced /etc/resolv.conf (e.g. malicious DHCP/VPN) - flagged for re-assessment given any Python code performing DNS resolution relies on this resolver. Fixed in glibc 2.43-6 (sid) - waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-8674

# Memory exhaustion in perl. Not exploitable; documented in POLICY_CONFIGURATION.md.
CVE-2026-82560

# Local privilege escalation (TOCTOU in dynamic loader) in glibc. Waiting for fix to be merged upstream and to be included in Debian release.
CVE-2026-86805

# Stack-based buffer overflow in glibc dynamic loader. Waiting for fix to be merged upstream and to be included in Debian release. Only exploitable by a local attacker against setuid/setgid (AT_SECURE) programs — limited scope.
CVE-2026-95818

# Use-after-free in libstdc++ binary heap erase_if (gcc-14). Only reachable from C++ code calling erase_if on that heap and linking the system libstdc++ - not used by CPython. Debian trixie unfixed (no-dsa, minor) - waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-102010

# Integer overflow in libstdc++ aligned operator new (gcc-14). Only reachable from C++ extension modules using over-aligned new with attacker-controlled sizes and the system libstdc++ - not used by CPython. Unfixed in Debian trixie and sid - waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-95619

# ==========================
# Python Issues
# ==========================

# Affected 3.12 only - fixed in 3.15, not backported to 3.12.
CVE-2025-15366
CVE-2025-15367
CVE-2025-12781

# Affected 3.12, 3.13 - fixed in 3.13.13, no 3.12 backport available yet. Only exploitable when parsing untrusted base64 data with `base64.b64decode()`. Use `validate=True` to mitigate.
CVE-2026-3446

# Affected 3.12, 3.14 - fixed in 3.13.14, 3.14.5rc1, 3.15.0b1. No 3.12 backport available yet.
CVE-2026-6019

# Affected 3.12, 3.13, 3.14 - fixed in 3.15.0; backports merged to 3.13 and 3.14 (PR #158429, #158430) but not yet released, 3.12 backports reverted. Only exploitable locally when the temp tree is attacker-writable during cleanup.
CVE-2026-12345

# ==========================
# pip vendored dependency issues
# ==========================

# Outdated msgpack bundled inside pip's own pip/_vendor/msgpack (pip 26.2, the latest release). Not the top-level msgpack package, which is already pinned to the fixed 1.2.1 release in the Dockerfile. Only used internally by pip's HTTP cache; waiting for pip to update its vendored copy.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# Outdated setuptools referenced in pip's own pip/_vendor/vendor.txt (pip 26.2, the latest release). Not the top-level setuptools package, which is already pinned to the fixed 83.0.0 release in the Dockerfile. Waiting for pip to update its vendored reference.
CVE-2025-47273
CVE-2026-59890

# urllib3 2.7.0 vendored in pip/_vendor/urllib3 (pip 26.2.1) - fixed in urllib3 2.8.0. Only used by pip at build time; waiting for pip to update its vendored copy.
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97688
CVE-2026-97689
